   "subject": "Re: Interpretation variograms",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Elke,</div><div><br></div><div>If you turn the collars off every day, then there is going to be some daily structure that shows up in the variogram/periodogram, but those variograms all look range resident, regardless. The peaks don&#39;t keep increasing with time lag. The question is whether or not there is periodicity, which could be addressed with model selection, following <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">vignette(&#39;variogram&#39;)</span>, if that&#39;s of interest.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Chris<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Monday, September 16, 2019 at 3:17:35 PM UTC-4, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">elkesc...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Christen,</div><div><br></div><div>I am new to telemetry analysis with ctmm. We have been studying movement of free-ranging owned dogs in southern Chile with continuous data (each 10 min was programmed), during 3 week intervals app. I am currently struggeling with the interpretation of some variograms to decide whether I can classify the dogs as range residents or not. There is always some amount of periodicity as the GPS turned off when dogs where sleeping. Would it be possible you help us with the interpretation of range residency of the attached variograms? I also provide one exemplary periodogram.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks so much in advance for your answer,</div><div>cheers</div><div>Elke<br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ctmm-user/attach/24ed05e1d7d84/Toby_fall_N=124.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"Toby_fall_N=124.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"208\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ctmm-user/attach/24ed05e1d7d84/Sofie_summer_N=669.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"Sofie_summer_N=669.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"208\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ctmm-user/attach/24ed05e1d7d84/Lobo_winter_N=350.png?part=0.3&amp;view=1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"Lobo_winter_N=350.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"208\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ctmm-user/attach/24ed0